                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>landscape painter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This could refer to William Mulready's mother, about whom the DNB says
                            little is known, save that she lives until at least 1811, when she
                            modelled for John Linnell, and William Mulready's wife, Elizabeth
                            Robinson Varley, whom Mulready married when he was 17 (12 July 1803) and
                            she was 19. They had 4 sons (b. Paul 1804, William 1805, Michael 1807,
                            and John 1809), although it is said to have been an unhappy marriage. In
                            the absence of exact dates of birth, which might have allowed us a sense
                            of when Elizabeth was 'visitable' it is difficult to be certain. Most
                            are calls on - and it seems likley that these are references to
                            Mulready's wife.</p>
                    </note>
